A colleague's risk script computes the maximum drawdown, in pounds, of 10 years of daily closing prices like this:

```python
def max_drawdown(prices):
    worst = 0
    for i in range(len(prices)):
        for j in range(i + 1, len(prices)):
            worst = max(worst, prices[i] - prices[j])
    return worst
```

(a) Say what it costs for about 2,520 prices, in big O and in rough numbers. (b) Write a one-pass version and argue why it is correct. (c) Explain how it relates to the best single trade and to the maximum subarray. (d) Name two edge cases and what your function returns. (e) The report now needs the drawdown inside each of 1,000 date ranges. Say what you would precompute, and what stays hard.
